{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc | sed -n '415,445p'; nl -ba src/cljc/dao/await.cljc | sed -n '175,250p'\"","aggregated_output":"   415\t   `stream` module registered in its registry.  No telemetry stream is\n   416\t   installed, and the VM owns no program medium: `make-session` builds the\n   417\t   medium, its attachment, the observer, and the VM together.\n   418\t\n   419\t   `extra-primitives` is the host-supplied map merged over the REPL's own\n   420\t   primitives, so an embedding host's functions win a name collision.\"\n   421\t  ([vm-type output-stream] (make-vm vm-type output-stream nil))\n   422\t  ([vm-type output-stream extra-primitives]\n   423\t   (when-not (contains? vm-constructors vm-type)\n   424\t     (throw (ex-info \"Unknown Yin REPL VM type\"\n   425\t                     {:vm-type vm-type\n   426\t                      :supported (vec (keys vm-constructors))})))\n   427\t   ((get vm-constructors vm-type)\n   428\t    {:primitives (merge (make-repl-primitives output-stream) extra-primitives)\n   429\t     :modules (module/register-stream-module (module/default-registry))\n   430\t     :make-stream make-ring-stream\n   431\t     ;; the task's capability secret (yin.vm.linker.md 7.3, r10): the REPL\n   432\t     ;; is the composition, so it mints one from its own random source,\n   433\t     ;; and a fresh one for every install child the task starts\n   434\t     :capability-secret (str (random-uuid))\n   435\t     :secret-source (fn [_origin] (str (random-uuid)))})))\n   436\t\n   437\t\n   438\t(defn- make-runner\n   439\t  \"The run step the evaluator observer hands each loaded program: run the\n   440\t   VM through its protocol entry point, as a plain function so it can be\n   441\t   handed to observer coordination on every host, and answer a halted\n   442\t   run's value on `output-stream` under `round`.  The shell reads the value\n   443\t   from that stream, never from the VM record; the append outcome rides\n   444\t   back on the VM as `::result-append`, so a refused append is reported\n   445\t   rather than silently lost.\"\n   175\t(defn- host-stream?\n   176\t  \"True when v is a dao.stream handle (declares a reader or writer\n   177\t   surface).\"\n   178\t  [v]\n   179\t  (or (ds/reader? v) (ds/writer? v)))\n   180\t\n   181\t\n   182\t(defn- attach-env-streams\n   183\t  \"Attach every v2 handle in the user env to `vm`: the handle goes into the\n   184\t   VM's private `:resources` table and the env value becomes the sealed\n   185\t   stream reference the engine issues for it (yin.vm.linker.md section\n   186\t   7.3, r8 and r10). Non-handle values pass through unchanged.\"\n   187\t  [vm env]\n   188\t  (reduce-kv (fn [vm sym v]\n   189\t               (if (host-stream? v)\n   190\t                 (let [[ref vm] (engine/attach-resource vm v)]\n   191\t                   (assoc-in vm [:env sym] ref))\n   192\t                 vm))\n   193\t             vm\n   194\t             env))\n   195\t\n   196\t\n   197\t(defn- result-map\n   198\t  [proc vm-state]\n   199\t  {:type :dao.await/result,\n   200\t   :vm vm-state,\n   201\t   :value (vm/value vm-state),\n   202\t   :blocked? (vm/blocked? vm-state),\n   203\t   :proc proc})\n   204\t\n   205\t\n   206\t(defn run\n   207\t  \"Drive a process on a fresh yin.vm ast-walker VM until it returns a\n   208\t   value or parks on a stream effect.\n   209\t\n   210\t   opts are host-composition options passed to yin.vm.ast-walker/create-vm\n   211\t   (:make-stream, :primitives, :call-in/:call-out, :bridge,\n   212\t   :capability-secret). :env always comes from the process, and :modules is\n   213\t   the caller's registry with the await bindings layered on top, so await\n   214\t   names always resolve. `run` is the composition of the task it makes, so\n   215\t   absent a supplied `:capability-secret` it mints one from its own random\n   216\t   source (yin.vm.linker.md section 7.3, r10), and absent a supplied\n   217\t   `:secret-source` it mints a fresh secret for each install child.\n   218\t\n   219\t   Returns a result map:\n   220\t     {:type :dao.await/result\n   221\t      :vm   <vm state>\n   222\t      :value <result-value | :yin/blocked>\n   223\t      :blocked? <bool>\n   224\t      :proc <original process descriptor>}\n   225\t\n   226\t   A blocked process is resumed with (await/resume result) once the host has\n   227\t   appended to (or closed) the stream a parked entry is waiting on.\"\n   228\t  ([proc] (run proc {}))\n   229\t  ([proc opts]\n   230\t   (let [env (vm/check-bindings! :env (:env proc))\n   231\t         vm (-> (ast-walker/create-vm\n   232\t                  (assoc opts\n   233\t                         :modules (registry (:modules opts))\n   234\t                         :capability-secret (or (:capability-secret opts)\n   235\t                                                (str (random-uuid)))\n   236\t                         ;; each install child's secret, fresh, unless the\n   237\t                         ;; caller injects its own source\n   238\t                         :secret-source (or (:secret-source opts)\n   239\t                                            (fn [_origin]\n   240\t                                              (str (random-uuid))))\n   241\t                         :env (into {} (remove #(host-stream? (val %))) env)))\n   242\t                (attach-env-streams env))\n   243\t         after (vm/eval vm (:ast proc))]\n   244\t     (result-map proc after))))\n   245\t\n   246\t\n   247\t(defn resume\n   248\t  \"Resume a blocked process by polling the wait set.\n   249\t\n   250\t   There is no wake list to hand over (v1's :woke came from dao.stream\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat collab/1790434200000-vm-engineer-linker-m4-s3c-child-secrets.claude-opus-5-5.report.md'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat collab/1790434200000-vm-engineer-linker-m4-s3c-child-secrets.claude-opus-5-5.report.md'","aggregated_output":"Completed-GMT: 2026-09-26 12:03:17 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-09-26 19:03:17 +07\nCreated-GMT: 2026-09-26 12:35:00 GMT\nCreated-Local: 2026-09-26 19:35:00 +0700\nCoding-Agent: claude\nSession-ID: 59731830-4c7a-442c-ab9a-350c68c8a122 (resumed)\n\n# Report: S3c, the REPL and dao.await compositions mint install children's secrets\n\nWorktree: /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-m4-s3 (branch m4-s3, uncommitted).\n\nThe clocks disagree: `date` reported 12:03:17 GMT when I finished, earlier\nthan the brief's Created-GMT of 12:35:00. I have recorded what `date` gave.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe re-gate's P1 is fixed. Both compositions now supply a source that\nmints a fresh secret for each install child. The engine is unchanged and\nstill uses no clock and no RNG: it only calls the composition's source.\n\n## The fix\n\nThe whole diff is two source edits:\n\n- **`src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc`** (`make-vm`): beside the root\n  `:capability-secret`, it now passes `:secret-source (fn [_origin] (str\n  (random-uuid)))`. The REPL is the composition, and this is its own\n  random source.\n- **`src/cljc/dao/await.cljc`** (`run`): it passes `:secret-source (or\n  (:secret-source opts) (fn [_origin] (str (random-uuid))))`. A caller\n  can still inject its own source, which keeps tests deterministic. The\n  docstring says so.\n\n## Tests added (in `test/yin/vm/linker_require_test.cljc`)\n\nBoth end-to-end tests install the same module. Its body makes a stream,\nwrites 7, and reads it back through a cursor, so the install child must\nissue both a stream reference and a cursor reference.\n\n- **`a-stream-using-module-installs-through-the-repl-composition-test`**\n  - It builds the task with `yin.repl/make-vm :ast-walker`. Only the link\n    pair is added, because the shell does not wire one until M5. The\n    stub responder answers the link request.\n  - It asserts the task carries a secret source, and that the program\n    resumes with 7.\n- **`a-stream-using-module-installs-through-dao-await-test`**\n  - It drives `await/run` and `await/resume` with the link pair in the\n    options, and asserts the default source is present and the value is\n    7.\n  - A second case injects a caller source. It asserts that source was\n    the one used, minting exactly one child secret, for origin `:t0.0`.\n- **Deliberately omitted source.** The existing test is kept unchanged:\n  `a-reference-lowers-only-where-it-can-attach-test`, in its \"a child\n  minted no secret can issue no reference\" case. It builds a composition\n  with `:secret-source nil`, and the install is refused with\n  `:no-capability-secret`.\n\nI did not watch the new tests fail against the old code. Without the fix,\nthe child has no secret, so `issue-ref` refuses its `stream/make` with\n`:no-capability-secret` and both installs are refused.\n\n## Checks\n\n- **JVM, touched namespaces only.** 91 tests / 1,038 assertions, 0\n  failures, 0 errors:\n  - `yin.vm.linker-require-test`: 26 tests / 503 assertions;\n  - `dao.await-test`, `yin.repl-test` and\n    `yang.clojure.stream-eval-test`: 65 tests / 535 assertions.\n- **clj-kondo** (via `mise exec -- clojure -M:kondo`) on every changed\n  file: 0 errors. The remaining warnings are the known pre-existing ones.\n- **cljstyle**: clean.\n- **ASCII and 80 columns** on added lines: 0 violations.\n\n## Observation: a stream kept in a module's store still needs an attacher\n\nA module that keeps a stream reference in its own store (for example\n`(def s (stream/make))`) exports that store snapshot. Lowering it needs\nthe receiver's `:attach-stream`, which neither the REPL nor `dao.await`\nsupplies, so such an install fails closed with `:yin.k/unsatisfied` (r9).\nThe module in these tests uses its stream through a local binding, so its\nstore holds only the value 7.\n\nWiring an attacher would mean these compositions keep a directory of the\nstreams they create. That is outside this brief, so I left it for M5 or a\nlater fix.\n\n## Unrun\n\n- The full JVM, Node, and Dart lanes (the orchestrator runs them).\n\nStatus: COMPLETE\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
