{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"agent_message","text":"The prior P1 is closed. The REPL and `dao.await` now give each install child a secret from a composition supplied source ([repl.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-m4-s3/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:427), [await.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-m4-s3/src/cljc/dao/await.cljc:229)). The engine only calls that source; it does not use an RNG or clock ([engine.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-m4-s3/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:910)). `random-uuid` is available on the JVM, ClojureScript, and the pinned ClojureDart runtime.\n\nThe new tests install a child that issues **both** a stream reference and a cursor reference, then writes and reads through them via each composition ([linker_require_test.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-m4-s3/test/yin/vm/linker_require_test.cljc:1229), [REPL case](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-m4-s3/test/yin/vm/linker_require_test.cljc:1250), [await case](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-m4-s3/test/yin/vm/linker_require_test.cljc:1281)). The omitted-source refusal remains covered ([linker_require_test.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-m4-s3/test/yin/vm/linker_require_test.cljc:890)). Child secrets come from fresh UUID calls rather than the predictable origin tag; references are authenticated on use and lift, and lift encodes resource markers without seals ([engine.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-m4-s3/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:242), [engine.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-m4-s3/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:545)).\n\nThe reported JVM and lint results are green. I did not rerun suites; Node and Dart results were still pending in the supplied evidence. The new test file is currently **untracked**, so it must be included when the change is committed.\n\n**Verdict: APPROVE. Must-fix list: none.**"}}
